    "text": "The government shutdown has frozen the Small Business Administration’s lending programs across the country. Joining NTD to discuss are Javier Palomarez, founder and CEO of the U.S. Hispanic Business Council and former Obama campaign adviser, and Vance Ginn, president of Ginn Economic Consulting and former chief economist of the White House's Office of Management and Budget.\nPanel Analysis: Small Business Administration Lending Programs Frozen Amid Shutdown, Impact on Businesses and Economy\nJavier Palomarez and Vance Ginn discussed the government shutdown causing the Small Business Administration to freeze its lending programs.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/22/2025, 11:58:54 PM EDT",
